        "table": "Electrical characteristics",
        "note": "VBE(sat) 0.65 V to 0.85 V at IC = 10 mA, IB = 1.0 mA."
      },
      "confidence": "derived",
      "derivation": "IS from the base-emitter saturation voltage: VBE(sat) is 0.65 V to 0.85 V at IC = 10 mA, IB = 1 mA, so the midpoint 0.75 V carries IE = 11 mA through the emitter junction, IS·e^(VBE/Vt)·(1 + 1/βF) = IE with βF = 200 and n = 1; the collector junction's share, e^(−VCE(sat)/Vt), is under 0.1 % and left out. IS = 2.2993e-15 A at Vt = 25.693 mV.",
      "note": {
        "en": "onsemi publishes no SPICE model on this sheet, so IS is fitted from the one table row that puts a junction voltage beside a current. It gives VBE = 0.689 V at 1 mA, a few tens of millivolts above what a bench meter reads on a real 2N3904.",
        "fr": "onsemi ne publie aucun modèle SPICE sur cette fiche : IS est donc ajusté sur la seule ligne du tableau qui met une tension de jonction en face d’un courant. Il donne VBE = 0.689 V à 1 mA, quelques dizaines de millivolts au-dessus de ce qu’un multimètre lit sur un vrai 2N3904."
      }
    },
    "br": {
      "value": 1,
      "dimensionless": true,
      "source": {
        "note": "Inverse-mode current gain, class-representative for a small-signal planar transistor: the 2N3904 sheet states none. Read only when the collector junction conducts, in saturation or with the part reversed."
      },
      "confidence": "typical",
      "note": {
        "en": "Ebers–Moll here has no collector resistance, so in saturation it reads VCE(sat) near 65 mV at a forced gain of ten, where the sheet guarantees ≤ 0.2 V: the ohmic drop is what the model leaves out.",
        "fr": "Ebers–Moll n’a ici aucune résistance de collecteur : en saturation il lit VCE(sat) près de 65 mV pour un gain forcé de dix, quand la fiche garantit ≤ 0.2 V. C’est la chute ohmique que le modèle omet."
      }
    },
